def agent_story():return '<div class="agent-story"><div class="agent-copy"><p class="eyebrow">THINK IT THROUGH. THEN FOLLOW THROUGH.</p><h2>From chat<br>to checked off.</h2><p>Give the next steps from your AI conversation a home in Todoer.</p><ul class="agent-benefits"><li>Capture an idea</li><li>Find an existing task</li><li>Update the next step</li></ul><a class="secondary" href="/agents.html">Connect your workflow →</a></div><div class="chat-demo"><span class="pill">Illustrative agent workflow</span><p class="chat-user">“Turn this launch plan into tasks in my Todoer inbox.”</p><div class="chat-reply"><span class="accent">Ready for your next step.</span><ul><li>Draft the announcement</li><li>Review the landing page</li><li>Prepare the launch checklist</li></ul></div><p class="fine">Compatible client and authorization required. <a href="/agents.html">Connection details →</a></p></div></div>'

preview=re.search(r'(<section id="preview".*?</section>)',pages['index'][2],re.S).group(1)
pages['index']=('A clearer head. A next step you can take.','Get tasks out of your head and into motion. Todoer connects everyday planning with optional AI-agent workflows.', '<section class="hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow">FOR EVERYTHING YOU KEEP MEANING TO DO</p><h1>A clearer head.<br><span>A real next step.</span></h1><p class="lead">The project. The small errand. That idea from your AI chat.<br>Get it out of your head, give it a place, and move it forward.</p><div class="actions">'+cta+'<a class="secondary" href="#story">Find your breathing room ↓</a></div><p class="fine">Your tasks, your pace. AI when you want it.</p></section>'+section('Less in your head.<br>More within reach.','<div id="story" class="thought-flow"><div class="thought-cloud"><span>The idea from that chat</span><span>The thing for tomorrow</span><span>That project you keep putting off</span></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="next-step"><span class="eyebrow">ONE PLACE. ONE NEXT STEP.</span><p>Pick it up.<br>Move it forward.</p><a href="/product.html">Meet your new workspace →</a></div></div>')+preview+section('Being organized can feel<br>lighter than this.',cards([('Catch the thought','Save it before it slips away. You can organize it later.'),('Make the next step obvious','Break a daunting project into small tasks, with the context right beside them.'),('Leave the day with less unfinished','See what matters today. Let the rest wait somewhere you can trust yourself to check.')]))+section('Keep the momentum<br>after the conversation.',agent_story())+section('You already know how to begin.',cards([('One inbox','Put the scattered thoughts in one place. A rough sentence is enough.'),('One small action','Pick something you can finish. Add the context you need, skip the ceremony.'),('One satisfying checkmark','Finish it. Come back tomorrow with a little less to carry.')]))+section('Small price.<br>A little more breathing room.','<div class="offer-strip"><div class="offer-intro"><span class="pill">PLANNED LAUNCH OFFER</span><p>Choose your rhythm.</p><a class="button" href="/pricing.html">Compare plans →</a></div><a href="/pricing.html" class="offer-option"><span>YEARLY</span><strong>€1<small>/month</small></strong><p>€12 billed annually</p></a><a href="/pricing.html" class="offer-option"><span>PERPETUAL</span><strong>€49<small> once</small></strong><p>Explore the one-time option →</p></a></div><p class="offer-footnote">Planned offers · Checkout not open · AI credits separate · Perpetual terms pending</p>')+section('A little more confidence<br>before you begin.',cards([('You can see the workflow','Explore concrete capture, planning and nested-task examples in our guides. No mystery about how you would use it.'),('AI stays optional','Use Todoer on its own. When you ask for built-in AI drafts, review them before applying.'),('Your work can travel','Export formats include text, CSV, JSON and ZIP. Keep your next move open.')]))+section('Good questions. Clear answers.',faq([('Can I manage tasks from Claude or ChatGPT?','Todoer provides MCP, REST and CLI access for compatible AI clients. You need an authorized connection. Specific hosted Claude and ChatGPT connector acceptance has not yet been verified; check client support before relying on it.'),('Do I have to build a productivity system first?','No. Start with an inbox and one list. Add sections, tags, nested tasks and a review routine only when they help.'),('Do I need AI credits for everyday tasks?','No. Core capture and planning do not need AI. Optional built-in AI usage would be purchased separately once credit sales are available.'),('Can I buy a plan now?','Not yet. The pricing page shows planned launch offers. Create an account where registration is available; paid checkout is not open.')])) )
pages['product']=('Everything in its place.<br>You, back in motion.','A focused home for your tasks, project context and next actions.',section('Less searching. More starting.',cards(features))+section('From “I should” to “it’s done.”','<div class="journey"><article><span>01 / CAPTURE</span><h3>Start messy.</h3><p>Save the idea as it comes. Keep the link, original wording or rough brief alongside the task.</p></article><article><span>02 / CLARIFY</span><h3>Make it doable.</h3><p>Give a project its own list. Split tasks into steps, add notes and files, and keep the details close.</p></article><article><span>03 / FOLLOW THROUGH</span><h3>Come back with a plan.</h3><p>Use Today, Upcoming and recurring tasks to find your rhythm. Review your lists before the next week begins.</p></article></div><a class="button" href="/guides.html">Find a workflow that fits →</a>')+section('And when your ideas begin in chat?',agent_story()))
pages['agents']=('Don’t leave your next step<br>buried in a chat.','Connect the thinking you do with AI to the work you want to finish.',section('A useful conversation deserves a follow-through.',agent_story())+section('Three ways to put an agent to work.',cards([('“Capture this for later.”','Save action items into a list so they are waiting when you return to your day.'),('“What is already on my list?”','Let an authorized compatible agent search your tasks and retrieve relevant context.'),('“Help me break this down.”','Use optional built-in assistance to draft a task tree. Edit it, review it and apply it deliberately.')]))+section('Connect deliberately. Keep control.', '<ol class="steps"><li><b>Choose a compatible client.</b> Todoer supports MCP and offers REST and CLI surfaces. Verify the features your client can use.</li><li><b>Authorize the connection.</b> Use the supported account authorization or scoped credentials. Never paste credentials into a public chat.</li><li><b>Start with one small task.</b> Ask for a capture, check where it landed, and build from there.</li></ol><p>Claude and ChatGPT are examples of AI environments people may want to use. Their hosted Todoer connector acceptance remains unverified. This is not a claim of an official partnership or one-click integration.</p><p>Built-in assistance sends your submitted brief or capture and eligible destination context to configured providers. External agents follow their own provider policies.</p><a href="/privacy.html">Read how data is handled →</a>'))
